1
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Where Hands Touch is a war, drama, romance film directed by Amma Asante.

2
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Germany, 1944.

3
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Leyna, the 15-year old daughter of a white German mother and a black African father, meets Lutz, a compassionate member of the Hitler
Youth whose father is a prominent Nazi soldier, and they form an unlikely connection in this quickly changing world.

4
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:30,000
Leyna, played by Amandla Stenberg.

5
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:36,000
Lutz, played by George MacKay.

6
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:42,000
Kerstin, played by Abbie Cornish.

7
00:42:42,000 --> 00:42:48,000
Heinz, played by Christopher Eccleston.

8
00:48:48,000 --> 00:48:54,000
Koen, played by Tom Sweet.

9
00:54:54,000 --> 00:55:00,000
Juttner, played by Alec Newman.

10
01:01:00,000 --> 01:01:06,000
Where Hands Touch is a 2018 romantic war drama film written and directed by Amma Asante and starring
Amandla Stenberg, George MacKay, Abbie Cornish, Christopher Eccleston, and Tom Sweet.

11
01:07:06,000 --> 01:07:12,000
It tells a fictional story of Leyna (Stenberg), a teenage girl under threat
because of her mixed heritage while surviving in Nazi Germany.

12
01:13:12,000 --> 01:13:18,000
The film is based on historical record of the
persecution of black people in Nazi Germany.

13
01:19:18,000 --> 01:19:24,000
The film is a British, Belgian, Canadian, and Irish co-production.

14
01:25:24,000 --> 01:25:30,000
Principal photography on the film began in November 2016 in Belgium
and lasted for a month, wrapping up in December 2016.

15
01:31:30,000 --> 01:31:36,000
Where Hands Touch premiered at the Toronto
International Film Festival on 9 September 2018.

16
01:37:36,000 --> 01:37:42,000
It was released theatrically in the United States on 14
September 2018 by Vertical Entertainment.

17
01:43:42,000 --> 01:43:48,000
It received mixed reviews, with praise directed at Stenberg's
performance, and criticism toward its screenplay.

18
01:49:48,000 --> 01:49:54,000
The film explores themes of nazi, jew persecution, hitler
youth, coming of age, interracial romance.

19
01:55:54,000 --> 01:56:00,000
The tone is emotional.
